      "canonicalConceptId": "concept:e783675c583d367f78f3cf55c294e5413c5a325df08b01277f6f589e473db6bd",
      "text": "Nigrostriatal dopamine modulates striatal circuitry involved in voluntary movement. This concept covers the direct, indirect and hyperdirect pathways, receptor signaling, and basal ganglia outputs. The cited circuit review describes their anatomy, while Cui and colleagues provide mouse evidence that qualifies a simple opposing-pathways account of movement. The axonal review highlights uncertainty about the sequence of early functional abnormalities and structural degeneration. These are educational circuit references; animal observations retain their experimental scope.",
