      "documentConcept": "Neurodegeneration mechanisms: proteostasis, mitochondria and neuroinflammation",
      "canonicalConceptId": "concept:970750f0cf1406b74712c25df21b19159d749967d6f059a6aaa17ba90e29867b",
      "text": "Research connects impaired protein degradation, mitochondrial quality control and inflammatory responses in Parkinson\u2019s disease. Patient-derived neuronal studies link dopamine oxidation to mitochondrial and lysosomal dysfunction. Mouse experiments distinguish basal mitochondrial turnover from stress-induced mitophagy and probe immune contributions to neuronal death. Human immune observations and model findings have different causal scope; pathway activation alone does not establish completed mitochondrial clearance.",
