      "documentConcept": "Sex, age and ancestry differences and young-onset PD",
      "canonicalConceptId": "concept:21d2e23a34a50a9a1867effbb320e0fc3cff9a4d64bfe85e264dc256a0bdd4e1",
      "text": "Age, sex and ancestry help describe variation in Parkinson\u2019s disease risk, while earlier onset is associated with distinct genetic, motor and social burdens. The task force recommends early-onset terminology and a standardized onset-age definition. Historical Medicare findings describe diagnosed disease rather than isolating genetic ancestry. Epidemiological interpretation requires attention to care access and the distinction between sociocultural categories and ancestry. Korean genetic association findings illustrate population-specific research while remaining limited by statistical power.",
